---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="CNH Hydraulic Quick Couplers | Hydraulic Quick Couplings" description="Hydraulic quick couplers for CNH machines — ISO 7241 / ISO 16028 flat-face / ISO 5675 profiles, sizes, threads and selection notes for CNH fleets.">
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">Machine-Compatible Quick Couplings</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">CNH Hydraulic Quick Couplers</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Source the right quick-disconnect couplings for CNH machines — attachment lines, implement outlets and service replacements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:text-navy-950 prose-h2:mt-10 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-a:text-brand-blue">
        <h2>CNH Machines and Their Hydraulic Quick Couplings</h2>
        <p>CNH Industrial is the parent of Case IH, New Holland and Steyr agricultural brands, plus Case Construction. Across the CNH family, tractor rear outlets use ISO 5675, construction loader auxiliaries use flat-face (ISO 16028 style), and older or service lines may carry ISO 7241 ball-lock couplings.</p>
        <h2>Coupling Profiles You Will Find on CNH Equipment</h2>
        <p>The table below summarises the quick-coupling profiles most commonly used across CNH machine families. It is a field guide, not a guarantee: verify the profile on your specific machine before ordering.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Machine family</th><th>Common profile</th><th>Typical sizes</th><th>Typical threads</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Tractor rear outlets (CNH brands)</td><td>ISO 5675 (agricultural)</td><td>1/2&quot; ISO 5675</td><td>BSPP / NPT</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Construction auxiliaries</td><td>Flat-face (ISO 16028 style)</td><td>1/2&quot; flat face</td><td>NPT / ORFS</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Service lines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>NPT / BSPP</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h2>Selection Notes for CNH Fleets</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Case IH, New Holland and Steyr tractors all use ISO 5675 on rear outlets.</li><li>Case and New Holland construction machines use flat-face loader auxiliaries.</li><li>CNH brands share industry-standard profiles — match by profile, not by badge.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Replacement and Service Guidance</h2>
        <p>CNH covers many brands; identify the actual machine brand and model first, then confirm the coupling profile. The CNH family follows industry standards across the board.</p>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Do all CNH tractor brands use ISO 5675?</h3><p>Yes — Case IH, New Holland and Steyr tractor rear outlets all use ISO 5675 agricultural couplings.</p><h3>Are CNH construction couplings flat-face?</h3><p>Case and New Holland loader auxiliaries use flat-face (ISO 16028 style) couplings on modern machines.</p><h3>Is CNH a coupling brand?</h3><p>No — CNH is the machine group. Their machines use industry-standard couplings sourced aftermarket.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-navy-950 p-8 text-center sm:p-10 lg:flex-row lg:text-left">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-white">Need Couplings for CNH Machines?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">Send the machine model, coupling profile or a photo — we confirm the match within 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="rounded-lg bg-cta-orange px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-orange-600">Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
